nge keeps the version; a breaking one raises it.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Changing an Event"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"HTTPDestinations","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}]},"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"GRDBPersistence"},"doc://LifecycleTracking/documentation/LifecycleTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/lifecycletracking","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"LifecycleTracking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and make the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker’s records durable as the app leaves the foreground."}]},"doc://AutomaticScreenTracking/documentation/AutomaticScreenTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track a screen view each time a screen’s view controller appears, without a modifier or a call on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each screen."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"AutomaticScreenTracking"},"doc://AppKitTracking/documentation/AppKitTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/appkittracking","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"AppKitTracking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Let AppKit views find their tracker up the responder chain, and track what controls do."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"Traffluent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Typed analytics events for Swift, delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}]},"doc://UIKitTracking/documentation/UIKitTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/uikittracking","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"UIKitTracking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hand UIKit views and view controllers their tracker as a trait, and track what controls do."}]},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that adds each tracked event to the span that was active when it was tracked."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"TracingDestinations"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TestingWhatYouTrack":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Automatic Tracking","abstract":[{"text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WritingAVendorDestination":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send events to an analytics vendor Traffluent doesn’t cover yet, from a module of your own, with the same rules as the destinations it ships."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination","role":"article","title":"Writing a Vendor Destination"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Sessions and Standard Context","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WhatGoesWhere":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/whatgoeswhere","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Four signals, four jobs. Decide which one a fact belongs to before you write the line that records it."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","role":"article","title":"Logging, Tracing, Metrics and Analytics"},"doc://SwiftUITracking/documentation/SwiftUITracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"SwiftUITracking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give SwiftUI views a tracker through the environment, and track what they do with view modifier